rried out in triplicate."},{"abbreviation_in_the_article":"Ru2","value":0.91,"value_relation":"=","std":0.1,"type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"water","temperature_C":37,"doi":"10.1039/d5qi00546a","year":2025,"counterion":"F[P-](F)(F)(F)(F)F","record_id":"MLDB-001409","detection":"UV-Vis","method_description":"Water–octanol partition coefficients were determined using the shake-flask method.57 A total of 1 mg of each complex was solubilized in 1000 μL of DMSO, and an aliquot of 50 μL was added to a mixture of equal volumes of water (975 μL) and n-octanol (975 μL). The solutions were continuously shaken for 24 h at 1000 rpm and 37 °C. Then, the samples were centrifuged for 5 min at 1000 rpm, and the organic and aqueous phases were separated. The organic phase was measured spectrophotometrically, and the concentration was determined from a calibration curve (linear regression) in order to obtain log P values = [complex(n-octanol)]/[complex(water)]. The experiments were carried out in triplicate."}],"ccdc":["RUPHIX","SUXTEO"]}